mment); if unused, prefer removing the step over conditionalizing it, and state that decision in the plan.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["golden-path job steps (lines 195-235) contain no jq invocation","scripts/probe_rebar.py:145-155 uses json.loads, not jq; comment 'the jq-pipeline analogue (empty output, not a raised error)'","external-integration.yml:283-285 comment: 'The golden-path probe is now Python — scripts/probe_rebar.py — and no longer needs jq itself.'"],"finding":"The plan optimizes the runtime of a jq-install step that appears to be dead: `jq` is never invoked anywhere in the golden-path job, whose only substantive steps are two pure-Python probes (scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py and scripts/probe_rebar.py). probe_rebar.py uses Python's json module and its own comment describes itself as 'the jq-pipeline analogue' in Python. The sibling external-integration.yml (lines 283-285) already documents that 'the golden-path probe is now Python ... and no longer needs jq itself.' Optimizing the setup time of an unused dependency is premature-optimization of the wrong target — the higher-value move is likely to DELETE the step, not conditionalize it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1bc87403f68dcd1a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml golden-path job (step 'Ensure jq is installed', line 207-208); Approach section","norm_id":"n0fed2eb80b3baedf","priority":0.625,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["The conditional edit ships, but the step still installs/checks a tool the job never uses — the optimized-but-unnecessary step persists indefinitely."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","